{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will set My face.</b> My wrath and My anger, like <i>and she had no face</i>. The meaning is that the survivors who have no sickness, if they go out against the enemies, they will be stricken before them, and sometimes they will flee with no pursuer, in the sense of <i>the camp of Aram</i> [fleeing without pursuit]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The citation מחנה ארם likely alludes to 2 Kings 7, where the Aramean camp fled though no one pursued; resolved by inference."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:44.086463110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}